From: mscharged-port
Subject: Type the friend code with the number keys
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native desktop convenience; the keypad behaves as before.

SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry enters a friend code with an on-screen keypad that
the Wii Remote's pointer presses. Natively the number keys of the top row
and the numeric keypad press the same buttons: every frame the screen takes
input, Update asks the host for the keys pressed since
(MSChargedTakeFriendCodeKey, src/platform/friend_code_keys.cpp) and passes
each to OnKeypadPointerPress for the pointer's player, so a key fills the
selected box and moves to the next one with the keypad's sound, as a press
of its button does. While the screen takes no input (its transitions, a
save, a popup) it does not ask, and the host drops keys once it has not asked
for a quarter of a second. Backspace and Enter keep their menu meanings, Back
and A. Console builds are unchanged.

